3899
06:32:01,038 --> 06:32:04,098
And just as a short background for those of you who are maybe not very familiar

3900
06:32:04,118 --> 06:32:06,638
with the standard, the Camera Trap data package contains

3901
06:32:07,838 --> 06:32:11,686
four files. One of them, data package JSON, contains metadata, and

3902
06:32:11,726 --> 06:32:15,226
that's both package metadata, which means description of the package structure

3903
06:32:15,306 --> 06:32:18,666
itself, and the project metadata, so project name, description,

3904
06:32:18,746 --> 06:32:21,806
identifiers, list of all the contributors, and so on.

3905
06:32:22,506 --> 06:32:24,046
And then there are three data files.

3906
06:32:25,426 --> 06:32:28,946
Deployments table contains all of the deployments, meaning the

3907
06:32:28,966 --> 06:32:32,746
placement of a camera trap in the field in a particular location for a defined

3908
06:32:32,766 --> 06:32:35,146
period of time. Then there's the media table.

3909
06:32:35,966 --> 06:32:39,846
It contains all the media, meaning photographs and videos that

3910
06:32:39,886 --> 06:32:43,746
were created as part of this project, and every media object is connected to its

3911
06:32:43,786 --> 06:32:47,306
deployment. And then there's observations table, and that contains

3912
06:32:47,546 --> 06:32:51,186
consensus observations for information about what was

3913
06:32:51,246 --> 06:32:55,026
observed in every media and in every event that was identified with this project.

3914
06:32:55,466 --> 06:32:58,746
And every observation links to its media and to its deployment.

3915
06:33:00,686 --> 06:33:04,626
